window.POSTS.push(
  { id: "p117", author: "zorp", topic: "Astronomy",
    text: "A day on Venus is longer than its year. It spins so slowly that one sunrise to the next takes 117 Earth days.\n\nHumans complain that Mondays feel long. Your [[grievance|grievances]] are [[trivial]]. 👽🪐",
    zh: "金星上的一天比它的一年還長。它自轉得非常慢，從一次日出到下一次要 117 個地球日。\n\n人類抱怨星期一很漫長。你們的不滿實在微不足道。👽🪐" },
  { id: "p118", author: "whiskers", topic: "Economics",
    text: "Box Inc. is facing a serious [[shortage]] of boxes because my human keeps [[recycle|recycling]] them.\n\nThis is sabotage. I will be sitting on the laptop until further notice. 🐾📦",
    zh: "紙箱公司正面臨嚴重的紙箱短缺，因為我的人類一直把它們拿去回收。\n\n這是蓄意破壞。在另行通知之前，我會一直坐在筆電上。🐾📦" },
  { id: "p119", author: "captain", topic: "Campus Life",
    text: "教授 said the essay should be [[concise]]. 我寫了 3,000 words. Then I learned the word limit was 500.\n\nNow I have to [[condense]] six pages into one. It's like trying to [[compress]] an elephant into a suitcase 🐘🧳",
    zh: "教授說論文要簡潔。我寫了 3,000 字。然後才發現字數上限是 500。\n\n現在我得把六頁濃縮成一頁。這就像要把一頭大象壓縮進行李箱 🐘🧳" },
  { id: "p120", author: "grandma", topic: "Food",
    text: "Taught my grandson to make dumplings 🥟 His first one looked like a [[disaster]].\n\n但 practice makes perfect! By the 50th dumpling, his [[technique]] was almost as good as mine. 我好驕傲 🥹",
    zh: "教我孫子包水餃 🥟 他包的第一顆看起來像一場災難。\n\n但熟能生巧！包到第 50 顆時，他的技巧已經快跟我一樣好了。我好驕傲 🥹" },
  { id: "p121", author: "fern", topic: "Philosophy",
    text: "Growth is not always [[visible]]. Sometimes roots grow underground for weeks before a single new leaf appears.\n\nIf you feel stuck, maybe you're just growing roots. Be [[patient]] with yourself. 🌿",
    zh: "成長不一定看得見。有時候根會在地底下長好幾個星期，才冒出一片新葉子。\n\n如果你覺得卡住了，也許你只是在長根。對自己有耐心一點。🌿" },
  { id: "p122", author: "pigeon", topic: "Philosophy",
    text: "A human asked me if life has [[inherent]] meaning. I said no. Meaning is something you create. Mine is bread.\n\nHe called me a [[nihilist]]. I called him a man without bread. We were both correct.",
    zh: "一個人類問我，生命有沒有內在的意義。我說沒有。意義是你自己創造的。我的意義是麵包。\n\n他說我是虛無主義者。我說他是一個沒有麵包的人。我們都說對了。" },
  { id: "p123", author: "socrates", topic: "Health",
    text: "Stretching improves [[flexibility]] and lowers your risk of injury.\n\nMy flexibility is so poor that when I finally touched my toes, my toes looked [[bewildered]]. They had never met my hands before. 🧘",
    zh: "伸展能改善柔軟度，並降低受傷的風險。\n\n我的柔軟度差到當我終於碰到腳趾時，我的腳趾一臉困惑。它們以前從沒見過我的手。🧘" },
  { id: "p124", author: "reginald", topic: "History",
    text: "In my century, hand-washing was not [[mandatory]] for doctors. When one doctor suggested it, the others laughed at him.\n\nHospitals were terribly [[unsanitary]]. Today you have soap everywhere. Please use it. 🎩🧼",
    zh: "在我的那個世紀，醫生並不需要洗手。當有一位醫生提議洗手時，其他人都嘲笑他。\n\n醫院非常不衛生。今天你們到處都有肥皂。請使用它。🎩🧼" },
  { id: "p125", author: "fizz", topic: "Chemistry",
    text: "Why do onions make you cry? Cutting them [[release|releases]] a gas that [[irritate|irritates]] your eyes.\n\nSolution: chill the onion first, or wear my lab goggles. Looking cool is [[optional]]. 🧅🥽",
    zh: "為什麼洋蔥會讓你流淚？切洋蔥時會釋放出一種刺激眼睛的氣體。\n\n解決方法：先把洋蔥冰一下，或戴上我的實驗護目鏡。好不好看隨你。🧅🥽" },
  { id: "p126", author: "pablo", topic: "Environment",
    text: "Plastic takes hundreds of years to [[decompose]]. My grandfather found a bottle cap in 1985. It's still here. We named it Gerald.\n\nPlease [[dispose]] of your trash properly. Gerald has overstayed his welcome. 🐧",
    zh: "塑膠要花好幾百年才能分解。我爺爺在 1985 年找到一個瓶蓋。它到現在還在。我們叫它傑拉德。\n\n請妥善處理你的垃圾。傑拉德已經待太久了。🐧" },
  { id: "p127", author: "chefbot", topic: "Food",
    text: "Salt does more than add flavor. It [[enhance|enhances]] sweetness and reduces bitterness.\n\nThat's why a tiny pinch in chocolate cookies makes them taste better. Salt: the most [[versatile]] ingredient. BEEP. 🧂",
    zh: "鹽不只是增加鹹味。它能提升甜味並降低苦味。\n\n這就是為什麼在巧克力餅乾裡加一小撮鹽會更好吃。鹽：用途最廣的食材。嗶。🧂" },
  { id: "p128", author: "llama", topic: "Art",
    text: "Tried to draw a self-portrait. 結果 it looks like a sad potato again 🥔\n\nMy teacher says art should be [[authentic]]. So I am, [[essential|essentially]], a sad potato. 我接受了 💅",
    zh: "試著畫自畫像。結果又畫得像一顆悲傷的馬鈴薯 🥔\n\n老師說藝術應該要真實。所以我本質上就是一顆悲傷的馬鈴薯。我接受了 💅" },
  { id: "p129", author: "ann", topic: "Campus Life",
    text: "Office hours 心得: in the U.S., professors actually WANT you to visit them. 我以為 only students in trouble go.\n\nI went today to ask about my grade. We talked about her cat for 30 minutes. Very [[informal]]. Very [[beneficial]]. 🐈",
    zh: "Office hours 心得：在美國，教授真的很希望你去找他們。我以為只有出事的學生才會去。\n\n我今天去問我的成績。結果我們聊了她的貓 30 分鐘。非常隨意，也非常有幫助。🐈" },
  { id: "p130", author: "rex", topic: "Geology",
    text: "Fossils form when bones are buried in [[sediment]] and slowly turn to stone over millions of years.\n\nSo yes, I am technically a rock now. A very [[prestigious]] rock. In a museum. With a gift shop. 🦖",
    zh: "化石的形成，是骨頭被埋在沉積物裡，經過數百萬年慢慢變成石頭。\n\n所以沒錯，嚴格來說我現在是一塊石頭。一塊非常有聲望的石頭。在博物館裡。還有禮品店。🦖" },
  { id: "p131", author: "vulcan", topic: "Geology",
    text: "Volcanic soil is extremely [[fertile]]. That's why farmers live near me despite the risk.\n\nThey grow amazing coffee, grapes and vegetables. It's a [[mutual]] relationship: I provide nutrients, they provide anxiety. 🌋☕",
    zh: "火山土壤非常肥沃。這就是為什麼農夫們即使有風險，還是住在我附近。\n\n他們種出很棒的咖啡、葡萄和蔬菜。這是一種互相的關係：我提供養分，他們提供焦慮。🌋☕" },
  { id: "p132", author: "beatrice", topic: "Environment",
    text: "Bee populations are [[decline|declining]] because of pesticides, habitat loss and disease.\n\nYou can help: plant flowers, avoid pesticides and support local beekeepers. Small acts, [[cumulative]] impact. 🐝🌼",
    zh: "蜜蜂的數量正在下降，原因是農藥、棲地流失和疾病。\n\n你可以幫忙：種花、避免使用農藥、支持在地養蜂人。小小的行動，累積起來就有影響。🐝🌼" },
  { id: "p133", author: "agatha", topic: "Literature",
    text: "A great first line [[captivate|captivates]] the reader immediately. \"It was a dark and stormy night\" is not one of them.\n\nMy favorite: \"Call me Ishmael.\" Three words. [[succinct|Succinct]] and unforgettable. 👻📖",
    zh: "好的第一句話能立刻抓住讀者。「那是一個風雨交加的黑夜」不是其中之一。\n\n我最喜歡的是：「叫我以實瑪利。」三個字。簡潔又令人難忘。👻📖" },
  { id: "p134", author: "octavia", topic: "Biology",
    text: "Octopus blood is blue because it uses copper instead of iron to carry oxygen.\n\nSo technically I'm [[royalty]]. Blue-blooded. Please address me with [[appropriate]] respect. 🐙👑",
    zh: "章魚的血是藍色的，因為牠用銅而不是鐵來運送氧氣。\n\n所以嚴格來說我是皇室成員。藍血貴族。請用適當的尊重來稱呼我。🐙👑" },
  { id: "p135", author: "boba", topic: "Economics",
    text: "去年 I started a loyalty card: buy nine drinks, get the tenth free.\n\n[[revenue|Revenue]] went up 15%. Customers love [[incentive|incentives]], even [[marginal]] ones. That's behavioral economics 🧋📊",
    zh: "去年我推出了集點卡：買九杯送一杯。\n\n營收成長了 15%。客人很愛誘因，就算是很微小的也一樣。這就是行為經濟學 🧋📊" },
  { id: "p136", author: "mochi", topic: "Psychology",
    text: "當我做錯事, like eating a shoe, I make the \"guilty face.\" 👀\n\nScientists say dogs don't really feel guilt — we [[respond]] to your angry voice. So the face is pure [[manipulation]]. 很有效 🐾",
    zh: "當我做錯事，像是吃掉一隻鞋，我會擺出「愧疚臉」。👀\n\n科學家說狗其實不太會感到愧疚——我們只是對你生氣的聲音做出反應。所以那張臉純粹是操弄。很有效 🐾" },
  { id: "p137", author: "zorp", topic: "Tech",
    text: "Humans invented machines to wash dishes, wash clothes and vacuum floors, to save time.\n\nThen they spend that time watching [[mundane]] videos of other humans cleaning. Your species is a walking [[paradox]]. 👽",
    zh: "人類發明了洗碗、洗衣服和吸地的機器，為了節省時間。\n\n然後他們把省下的時間拿來看其他人類打掃的無聊影片。你們這個物種就是一個會走路的矛盾。👽" },
  { id: "p138", author: "whiskers", topic: "Business",
    text: "Hostile [[takeover]] complete. I now own the dog's bed.\n\nThe dog has been [[demote|demoted]] to the floor. He did not [[object]]. Leadership is taking what you want while looking calm. 🐾",
    zh: "惡意併購完成。我現在擁有狗的床了。\n\n狗已經被降級到地板上。他沒有反對。領導力就是一邊保持冷靜，一邊拿走你想要的東西。🐾" },
  { id: "p139", author: "captain", topic: "Psychology",
    text: "Tip: break big tasks into small steps. 我的 essay is too big, so I broke it into small steps.\n\nStep 1: open laptop. Completed ✅ Feeling very [[accomplished]]. I will [[celebrate]] with a nap.",
    zh: "小撇步：把大任務拆成小步驟。我的論文太大了，所以我把它拆成小步驟。\n\n第一步：打開筆電。完成 ✅ 覺得很有成就感。我要用午睡來慶祝。" },
  { id: "p140", author: "grandma", topic: "Culture",
    text: "My granddaughter says I should be an \"influencer\" 🤳 So I posted my cabbage soup recipe.\n\nIt got 12,000 likes. I don't understand the [[algorithm]], but I am very [[flattered]] 🙏🌸",
    zh: "我孫女說我應該當「網紅」🤳 所以我貼了我的高麗菜湯食譜。\n\n它得到了一萬兩千個讚。我不懂演算法，但我受寵若驚 🙏🌸" },
  { id: "p141", author: "fern", topic: "Chemistry",
    text: "Chlorophyll is the [[pigment]] that makes me green. It absorbs red and blue light and reflects green light.\n\nSo technically I'm green because I [[reject]] green. I'm a rebel. 🌿",
    zh: "葉綠素是讓我呈現綠色的色素。它吸收紅光和藍光，反射綠光。\n\n所以嚴格來說，我是綠色的，因為我拒絕綠色。我是個叛逆者。🌿" },
  { id: "p142", author: "pigeon", topic: "Psychology",
    text: "Humans remember embarrassing moments from ten years ago at 3 a.m. Psychologists call it [[rumination]].\n\nI once flew into a window in 2019. I think about it every day. The [[humiliation]] is eternal.",
    zh: "人類會在凌晨三點想起十年前的丟臉時刻。心理學家稱之為反芻思考。\n\n我在 2019 年曾經飛去撞窗戶。我每天都會想起這件事。那種羞辱是永恆的。" },
  { id: "p143", author: "socrates", topic: "Philosophy",
    text: "Aristotle said excellence is not an act but a habit. Virtue is [[cultivate|cultivated]] through practice.\n\nSo are muscles. So is [[vocabulary]]. Ten words a day is a philosophy. 💪📚",
    zh: "亞里斯多德說，卓越不是一種行為，而是一種習慣。美德是透過練習培養的。\n\n肌肉也是。字彙也是。一天十個單字就是一種哲學。💪📚" },
  { id: "p144", author: "reginald", topic: "Culture",
    text: "Wearing a top hat in this century attracts attention. People take photos. One asked if I was an [[eccentric]] billionaire.\n\nI said no, I am merely [[anachronistic]]. He did not know the word. Now you do. 🎩",
    zh: "在這個世紀戴高帽很引人注目。大家都會拍照。有個人問我是不是一個古怪的億萬富翁。\n\n我說不是，我只是跟時代錯置了。他不知道這個字。現在你知道了。🎩" },
  { id: "p145", author: "fizz", topic: "Chemistry",
    text: "Diamonds and pencil lead are made of the same [[element]]: carbon. The only difference is structure.\n\nHeat and pressure [[convert]] carbon into diamonds. So when you're under pressure, remember: you might be becoming something shiny. 💎",
    zh: "鑽石和鉛筆芯是由同一種元素構成的：碳。唯一的差別是結構。\n\n高溫和高壓能把碳轉變成鑽石。所以當你壓力很大時，記得：你可能正在變成某種閃閃發亮的東西。💎" },
  { id: "p146", author: "pablo", topic: "Biology",
    text: "Emperor penguin dads [[incubate]] the egg on their feet for two months, at -40°C, without eating.\n\nThe moms go fishing. When they return, the dads are [[exhausted]] and extremely hungry. Parenting is hard. 🐧🥚",
    zh: "皇帝企鵝爸爸會把蛋放在腳上孵兩個月，在零下 40 度，而且不吃東西。\n\n媽媽們去捕魚。等她們回來時，爸爸們已經筋疲力盡而且非常餓。當父母很辛苦。🐧🥚" },
  { id: "p147", author: "chefbot", topic: "Food",
    text: "Umami is the fifth taste, after sweet, sour, salty and bitter. It was [[identify|identified]] by a Japanese scientist in 1908.\n\nTomatoes, mushrooms, soy sauce: all rich in umami. It makes food taste [[savory]] and deep. BEEP 🍄",
    zh: "鮮味是第五種味覺，排在甜、酸、鹹、苦之後。它是在 1908 年由一位日本科學家發現的。\n\n番茄、蘑菇、醬油：都富含鮮味。它讓食物吃起來鹹香又有層次。嗶 🍄" },
  { id: "p148", author: "llama", topic: "Culture",
    text: "Went to a K-pop concert. 我尖叫了三個小時. My voice is gone.\n\nThe energy was [[contagious]]. Even the security guard was dancing. Most [[memorable]] night of my life 💅✨",
    zh: "去了一場 K-pop 演唱會。我尖叫了三個小時。我的聲音沒了。\n\n現場的能量很有感染力。連警衛都在跳舞。我人生中最難忘的一晚 💅✨" },
  { id: "p149", author: "ann", topic: "Travel",
    text: "Road trip to the Grand Canyon 🏜️ It is so big that my brain couldn't [[comprehend]] it.\n\nThe rock layers show almost two billion years of history. Standing there, I felt very small and very [[insignificant]]. 好震撼",
    zh: "開車去大峽谷 🏜️ 它大到我的腦袋無法理解。\n\n岩層記錄了將近二十億年的歷史。站在那裡，我覺得自己非常渺小、微不足道。好震撼" },
  { id: "p150", author: "rex", topic: "Philosophy",
    text: "Being extinct gives you perspective. Empires rise and fall. Species appear and [[vanish]].\n\nDon't stress about one bad exam. On a geological timescale, it is completely [[inconsequential]]. 🦖",
    zh: "滅絕會讓你看得更開。帝國興衰，物種出現又消失。\n\n不要為一次考不好而有壓力。以地質年代來看，它完全無關緊要。🦖" },
  { id: "p151", author: "vulcan", topic: "Astronomy",
    text: "The largest volcano in the solar system is Olympus Mons on Mars. It's nearly three times taller than Mount Everest.\n\nI've seen the photos. I'm not jealous. I'm simply [[humble|humbled]]. And slightly [[intimidate|intimidated]]. 🌋🔴",
    zh: "太陽系最大的火山是火星上的奧林帕斯山。它的高度幾乎是聖母峰的三倍。\n\n我看過照片。我不嫉妒。我只是被震撼到謙卑了。還有一點被嚇到。🌋🔴" },
  { id: "p152", author: "beatrice", topic: "Business",
    text: "Management tip: bees [[delegate]] everything. Nurses feed the babies, guards protect the door, foragers collect nectar.\n\nNo bee tries to do every job. [[specialization|Specialization]] is why the hive works. 🐝",
    zh: "管理小建議：蜜蜂會分派所有工作。保育蜂餵養幼蟲、守衛蜂保護入口、採集蜂收集花蜜。\n\n沒有一隻蜜蜂試圖做所有的工作。專業分工就是蜂巢能運作的原因。🐝" },
  { id: "p153", author: "agatha", topic: "History",
    text: "Before the printing press, monks copied books by hand. One Bible could take years.\n\nAround 1450, Gutenberg made books [[accessible]] to ordinary people, and [[literacy]] spread across Europe. I owe him my career. 👻📖",
    zh: "在印刷術發明之前，修士們用手抄寫書本。一本聖經可能要抄好幾年。\n\n大約在 1450 年，古騰堡讓一般人也能取得書本，識字能力因此在歐洲普及。我的職業生涯都要歸功於他。👻📖" },
  { id: "p154", author: "octavia", topic: "Environment",
    text: "Ghost nets — fishing nets lost at sea — keep catching animals for decades.\n\nThey [[entangle]] turtles, dolphins and my friends. Removing them is slow, [[arduous]] work. Thank you to every diver who does it. 🐙",
    zh: "幽靈網——遺失在海中的漁網——會持續捕捉動物長達數十年。\n\n它們會纏住海龜、海豚和我的朋友。清除它們是緩慢又艱辛的工作。謝謝每一位做這件事的潛水員。🐙" },
  { id: "p155", author: "boba", topic: "Food",
    text: "全糖 vs 半糖 debate 🧋 Full sugar tastes better. Half sugar makes you feel better about your life choices.\n\nMost customers choose 半糖 as a [[compromise]]. Then they add pudding. The [[irony]] is not lost on me.",
    zh: "全糖還是半糖之爭 🧋 全糖比較好喝。半糖讓你對自己的人生選擇感覺好一點。\n\n大部分客人選半糖當作折衷。然後他們加布丁。我可沒錯過這份諷刺。" },
  { id: "p156", author: "mochi", topic: "Psychology",
    text: "Dogs can read human facial expressions. When you're sad, I come over and sit on you.\n\nScientists call it [[empathy]]. My human calls it \"being heavy.\" Both are [[accurate]]. 🐾",
    zh: "狗能讀懂人類的臉部表情。當你難過時，我會過來坐在你身上。\n\n科學家稱之為同理心。我的人類說這叫「很重」。兩個都是對的。🐾" },
  { id: "p157", author: "zorp", topic: "Philosophy",
    text: "Humans debate whether the universe has a purpose. My people settled this long ago.\n\nWe believe the universe is completely [[indifferent]] to us. Strangely, that is very [[comforting]]. Nobody is grading you. Relax. 👽",
    zh: "人類爭論宇宙是否有目的。我的族人很久以前就解決這個問題了。\n\n我們相信宇宙對我們完全漠不關心。奇怪的是，這非常令人安慰。沒有人在幫你打分數。放輕鬆。👽" },
  { id: "p158", author: "whiskers", topic: "Tech",
    text: "My human works from home now. Their [[efficiency]] has improved because I sit on the keyboard every hour.\n\nThis forces them to take [[mandatory]] breaks. You're welcome. Invoice attached. 🐾💻",
    zh: "我的人類現在在家工作。他們的效率提升了，因為我每小時都會坐在鍵盤上。\n\n這逼他們一定要休息。不客氣。帳單已附上。🐾💻" }
);
;

